    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d346">

                <pb facs="0402" n="394" sameAs="frus:frus1939v02/pg394"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.75/463b: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-04-10T18:00:00-05:00">April 10, 1939—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>24. Department’s 21, April 7, noon.<anchor n="38" xml:id="d346-f1"/> I assume
                    that upon receipt of the above telegram you immediately sought interviews with
                    the Turkish authorities and I am disappointed at the absence of reports from you
                    regarding Turkish reaction to European developments. In view of Turkey’s
                    outstanding strategic position it is vital for us to know what, if any action,
                    she may be contemplating in the present <pb facs="0403" n="395" xml:id="pg395"/>
                    threatening situation. If you have not already done so I hope that you will seek
                    interviews at once with officials in the Foreign Office and, if necessary, with
                    the Prime Minister and the President, report immediately their views, and
                    thereafter keep us informed of day to day developments as long as the present
                    crisis may last.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d346-f1" n="38" xml:id="d346-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it requested an early telegraphic report regarding attitude of
                    Turkish Government toward European situation with particular reference to
                    developments in Albania (765.75/463a).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
